# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Dated media register for the Great House Farm storyboard.

Every picture the player may show on a scene must be listed here with the date
of what it SHOWS (the newspaper's issue date, the photograph's date, the
document's date) -- never the upload date in a filename such as
"2026-02-09_consortium-newspaper..." or a WordPress /uploads/2026/10/ path.

Fields
  url       site path (/media/...) or absolute URL (wayback / wiki media)
  item      one id per underlying record, so copies of the same cutting dedupe
  title     caption shown in the player
  date      'YYYY', 'YYYY-MM' or 'YYYY-MM-DD'; None = date not established
  approx    True when the date is "c." (the check then allows one extra year)
  released  date a record was released/disclosed (e.g. an FOI reply); lets a
            records-era scene (2025+) show the record it is about
  basis     how the date was established (filename, caption, read off the image)
  exclude   reason the image is never shown on a slide (privacy, graphic, ...)
  allow_scenes  scene ids on which an UNDATED picture may be shown as a curated
            image, by Sion Buckler's express instruction only (caption says "undated")

Anything NOT in this register (for example the 293 undated family-album
photographs "Great House Farm Part 1-3 - NNN" on wayback) is undated and is
never placed on a dated slide. content/scene_media.py places media on scenes
by date and fails the build if any image falls outside its scene's period.
To add a new picture: add a row here with a date you can show, then rebuild.
"""

